UNIVERSALITY OF THE CHERRY: A_2 = p(p-1) for ANY circulant tournament
========================================================================
  p |  A_2 Paley  =p(p-1)? |    A_2 alt  =p(p-1)? | a4 Paley   a4 alt | a3 (both)
  7 |         42      True |         42      True |   0.1399  -0.0466 |         0
 11 |        110      True |        110      True |   0.1202   0.0721 |         0
 19 |        342      True |        342      True |   0.0840   0.0373 |         0
 23 |        506      True |        506      True |   0.0723   0.0039 |         0

=> A_2 = p(p-1) (cherry weight +1) holds IDENTICALLY for the non-QR tournament:
   it needs only g odd (the tournament condition), NOT the QR structure.
   a_4 -> 0 for both; a_3 = 0 for both. Same single generator => same limit e.

Exact R(p) = H * 2^{p-1}/p! for Paley vs the alt circulant tournament:
  p |   R Paley |     R alt   (both head to e=2.71828)
  7 |   2.40000 |   2.22222
 11 |   2.43951 |   2.37065
